      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, let's break down the steps:\n\n1. We first need to determine the total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10. This can be calculated using combinations, which is comb(10, 2).\n   - This gives us 45 ways of selecting members.\n\n2. Since there are 5 girls in the club, we need to calculate the number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5. This is further calculated using combinations, comb(5, 2).\n   - This gives us 10 ways for these selections.\n\n3. To find the probability of both selections being girls, we divide the number of ways girls can be chosen into the total number of ways to select any 2 members.\n   - Probability = 10 options / 45 total outcomes = 1/9.\n\n4. Hence, the given probability of selecting 2 girls out of 9 members is:\n   - \\boxed{\\frac{1}{9}}",
