      "text": "To find the probability that both members chosen are girls, use a combination of what you know about selecting girls out of the total members.  Pick 1 girl from the initial 10 members: $10$ choosers, $10$ choices.  Then pick the second girl from the remaining members: $9$ choosers, $9$ choices.  Since this process depends on 2 different choices, multiply the numbers: \n$$\\binom{10}{2} = \\binom{5}{2} \\cdot \\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{10!}{7!3!} = \\frac{10 \\cdot 9}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\boxed{45}.$$\n\nThe answer is: 45",
